From: Douglas Hellinger <doug.hellinger@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Nov 2017 22:48:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix tracerPid=0 in /proc

Always report TracerPid as 0 in /proc/<pid>/status, hiding ptrace
parent from userland.

Rebased for Linux 6.18.x (fs/proc/array.c).
---
 fs/proc/array.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/proc/array.c b/fs/proc/array.c
index 6f6fc16..bcf470d 100644
--- a/fs/proc/array.c
+++ b/fs/proc/array.c
@@ -159,7 +159,8 @@ static inline void task_state(struct seq_file *m, struct pid_namespace *ns,
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	tracer = ptrace_parent(p);
 	if (tracer)
-		tpid = task_pid_nr_ns(tracer, ns);
+		/* hide TracerPid */
+		tpid = 0;
 
 	ppid = task_ppid_nr_ns(p, ns);
 	tgid = task_tgid_nr_ns(p, ns);
-- 
2.43.0
